# Nia fork deltas

Before editing agent/desktop/portal paths, read the matching file under
`hermes-agent/docs/fork-deltas/` (branding, portal-gateway-billing,
providers-auto-router, desktop-packaging-updater, ui-lockdowns,
computer-use, SYNC-LOG). Entries are tagged `[agent]` / `[desktop]` /
`[portal]`.

## Must

- If a Nia delta changes, update that ledger file in the **same commit**.
- Before merging any upstream Hermes/Nous change: rebrand user-facing
  strings, window names, icons, bundle IDs, URLs, CLI help, telemetry
  endpoints, default provider (OkVevo portal), and update/channel URLs.
- Run `python3 scripts/check_nia_branding.py` before commits that touch
  user-facing product copy or identity files.
- Keep `LICENSE` / NOTICE / copyright attribution. Keep internal ids:
  `~/.hermes`, `hermes` CLI, `hermes://`, `HERMES_*`, Python module paths.
- Push only `okvevo` (`Jaikarans2003/OkVevo-Nia`). Never push `origin` (Nous).
- Land syncs on `staging` only after review. Follow
  `.cursor/plans/upstream-sync-v1_2559f0c6.plan.md` and the
  `upstream-sync` skill (explicit invoke; stops for approval).

## Do not

- Blind-merge `origin/main`.
- Strip attribution or rename wire/internal Hermes identifiers for fun.
- Treat Hermes Cloud / Nous billing / Skills Hub Nous origin as Nia product.
